    {
      "title": "How It Works",
      "content": "DSPy programs use <strong>natural language signatures</strong> to assign work to the language model. A DSPy signature is a tuple of input fields and output fields that tells DSPy what a text transformation needs to do. <strong>DSPy modules</strong> are task-adaptive components that abstract any particular text transformation, like answering a question or summarizing a paper. <strong>Teleprompters</strong> optimize all modules in the pipeline to maximize a metric.",
      "visualization": {
        "type": "flow-diagram",
        "description": "A flowchart showing the process of compiling a DSPy program, with teleprompters and modules interacting to optimize the pipeline.",
